NAME
     sysctl - read and write kernel settings

SYNOPSIS
     sysctl [-a] [-n] [-w] NAME[=VALUE]...
     sysctl -p [FILE]

DESCRIPTION
     sysctl reads and writes the knobs under /proc/sys: the hostname,
     the maximum number of processes, what a fault prints, and the rest.

OPTIONS
     -a          print everything there is
     -n          print the value without the name
     -w          write, rather than read
     -p [FILE]   apply the settings in FILE (/etc/sysctl.conf by default)

SEE ALSO
     /proc/sys, /etc/sysctl.conf
